# Initial Setup's Battery Monitor page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigBatteryMonitoring.cs.
#
# The claim: Activate reads the monitor type, the sensor, the board and the calibration numbers from
# the vehicle's parameters (ConfigBatteryMonitoring.cs:18-176), the timer puts the vehicle's own
# voltage and current beside them (:477-481), and a box is written to the vehicle when it is left -
# TXT_battcapacity_Validated calls setParam("BATT_CAPACITY", ...) (:184-203); there is no save
# button - and the vehicle echoes the new value. The value is put back at the end.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm, which sets
# BATT_MONITOR 4; the rest are the firmware's SITL defaults: BATT_CAPACITY 3300, BATT_VOLT_PIN 13,
# BATT_CURR_PIN 12, BATT_VOLT_MULT 10.1, BATT_AMP_PERVLT 17, SIM_BATT_VOLTAGE 12.6. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-battery.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# A run that stops half way leaves BATT_CAPACITY at 3400; the next run's first capacity expectation
# fails, and restoring it by hand (or re-running from a fresh SITL) puts it back.
#
# "MP Alert on Low Battery" reads and writes Settings.Instance - Mission Planner's config.xml, one
# dictionary with the Planner page's and Battery Monitor 2's keys (ConfigBatteryMonitoring.cs:53-60,
# 565-601). Ticking it puts speechbatteryenabled and speechenable in the dictionary at once and asks
# three InputBox questions whose answers go in too (config.<key> is the dictionary's own fact,
# settings.rs's); the page saves nothing, and after `restart` - which closes through the close box,
# which saves - the dictionary read back from the file holds them and the page opens ticked. The
# script has a config.xml of its own, so Mission Planner's is neither read nor written.

env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml

screen params
window 1600x1200
budget 30
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

# Initial Setup lists the page once every parameter is in (isConnected && gotAllParams,
# InitialSetup.cs:268-272), and here parameters are downloaded when asked for.
click param-download
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.BATT_MONITOR 4

click tab-setup
expect config.battery.open false
# Battery Monitor is the first Optional Hardware entry of InitialSetup's list.
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
click setup-page-ConfigBatteryMonitoring
expect config.battery.open true
expect config.battery.enabled true

# What Activate read. SITL's 17 A/V and 10.1 match no sensor in the table, so "0: Other", and its
# voltage pin 13 is "2: APM2.5+/ZealotF427 - 3DR Power Module" (:62-164).
expect config.battery.monitor 4
expect config.battery.monitor.text ~ Voltage and Current
expect config.battery.monitor.options >= 3
expect config.battery.sensor 0
expect config.battery.sensor.enabled true
expect config.battery.hwversion 2
expect config.battery.hwversion.enabled true
expect config.battery.capacity 3300
expect config.battery.divider 10.1
expect config.battery.ampspervolt 17
expect config.battery.calibration.enabled true
expect config.battery.divider.enabled true
expect config.battery.ampspervolt.enabled true

# The readouts: both voltage boxes open at cs.battery_voltage, and the timer has run at least once
# in the two seconds settled, filling the current (a double's text; SITL's disarmed current is not
# asserted beyond there being one).
expect config.battery.voltage ~ 12.
expect config.battery.measured ~ 12.
expect config.battery.readouts >= 1

# Activate's own writes - BATT_MONITOR, BATT_AMP_PERVLT and BATT_VOLT_MULT, each with the value the
# vehicle already holds (:172-173) - have all been answered, and nothing complained.
expect config.battery.writes.pending 0
expect config.battery.message none
expect params.value.BATT_VOLT_MULT 10.1
expect params.value.BATT_AMP_PERVLT 17

# The capacity to 3400: typed, then the box left for the divider box, which is what raises
# Validated. (Leaving the divider box later writes its unchanged 10.1 back, as the C# would.)
click battery-capacity
key ctrl+u
type 3400
click battery-divider
expect config.battery.capacity 3400
expect config.battery.write BATT_CAPACITY 3400 accepted
expect params.value.BATT_CAPACITY 3400
expect config.battery.message none

# And back.
click battery-capacity
key ctrl+u
type 3300
click battery-divider
expect config.battery.write BATT_CAPACITY 3300 accepted
expect params.value.BATT_CAPACITY 3300
expect params.value.BATT_VOLT_MULT 10.1
expect config.battery.message none

# The Sensor box is a DropDown combo: its text takes typing, which clears its selection and runs
# nothing - only SelectedIndexChanged is wired (ConfigBatteryMonitoring.Designer.cs:72-87). Clicking
# into it leaves the divider box, whose unchanged 10.1 is written back as before.
click battery-sensor
key BackSpace
type Z
expect config.battery.sensor.text 0: OtheZ
expect config.battery.sensor none
expect config.battery.list none
expect config.battery.writes.pending 0
expect config.battery.message none
# Its arrow drops the list; choosing "0: Other" is a change again, so its text comes back and the
# handler writes the divider and amps-per-volt the boxes hold - what the vehicle already has.
click battery-sensor-button
expect config.battery.list battery-sensor
click battery-sensor-0
expect config.battery.list none
expect config.battery.sensor 0
expect config.battery.sensor.text 0: Other
expect config.battery.writes.pending 0
expect config.battery.message none
expect params.value.BATT_VOLT_MULT 10.1
expect params.value.BATT_AMP_PERVLT 17
# The HW Ver box takes typing the same way, and writes nothing for it.
click battery-hw
key BackSpace
expect config.battery.hwversion.text 2: APM2.5+/ZealotF427 - 3DR Power Modul
expect config.battery.hwversion none
expect config.battery.writes.pending 0
expect params.value.BATT_VOLT_PIN 13
expect params.value.BATT_CURR_PIN 12

# The Low Battery alert. The script's config.xml has none of its keys: unticked, and the start-up
# save the only one.
expect config.battery.speech false
expect config.speechbatteryenabled none
expect config.saves 1
click battery-speech
expect config.battery.speech true
expect config.speechbatteryenabled True
expect config.speechenable True
expect config.battery.prompt ~ What do you want it to say
key ctrl+u
type LOW {batv}
key Return
expect config.speechbattery LOW {batv}
expect config.battery.prompt ~ What Voltage do you want to warn at
key ctrl+u
type 10.8
key Return
expect config.battery.prompt ~ What percentage do you want to warn at
key ctrl+u
type 25
key Return
expect config.battery.prompt none
expect config.speechbatteryvolt 10.8
expect config.speechbatterypercent 25
# InputBox keeps each answer too, URL-encoded under its caption and question (InputBox.cs:73-84,
# 178-184).
expect config.InputBoxNotificationWhatdoyouwantittosay LOW+%7Bbatv%7D
expect config.InputBoxBatteryLevelWhatVoltagedoyouwanttowarnat 10.8
expect config.InputBoxBatteryLevelWhatpercentagedoyouwanttowarnat 25
# In the dictionary, not yet in the file: the page saves nothing.
expect config.saves 1

# Choosing another page deactivates this one, as BackstageView does on every change.
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
expect config.battery.open false

# The close box saves config.xml; the new process reads it back before any page shows, and the
# page opens ticked from it.
restart
expect config.saved startup
expect config.error none
expect config.speechbatteryenabled True
expect config.speechenable True
expect config.speechbattery LOW {batv}
expect config.speechbatteryvolt 10.8
expect config.speechbatterypercent 25
expect config.InputBoxNotificationWhatdoyouwantittosay LOW+%7Bbatv%7D
expect config.InputBoxBatteryLevelWhatVoltagedoyouwanttowarnat 10.8
expect config.InputBoxBatteryLevelWhatpercentagedoyouwanttowarnat 25
click param-download
expect params.held > 1000
click tab-setup
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
click setup-page-ConfigBatteryMonitoring
expect config.battery.open true
expect config.battery.speech true
